`allow.hosts` contains `API.example.com`. Hosts are compared lower-case; a mixed-case entry is refused rather than normalised so that two implementations cannot differ on whether they normalise. SPEC §4.4: a host is a lower-case DNS name, an IPv4 literal or `localhost`, with an optional single leading `*.` label, or the bare `*`; two implementations must not disagree about what a host entry names.
